1
00:00:00,753 --> 00:00:04,007
The great thing about Ollama is that it has

2
00:00:04,199 --> 00:00:05,690
a quite powerful

3
00:00:06,267 --> 00:00:08,704
API that essentially allows you

4
00:00:09,249 --> 00:00:12,038
to do pretty much everything you can do with

5
00:00:12,198 --> 00:00:14,106
Ollama through the command line.

6
00:00:14,795 --> 00:00:17,344
So for example, create models, list

7
00:00:17,344 --> 00:00:19,123
available models, remove models.

8
00:00:19,893 --> 00:00:21,881
You can do all these things

9
00:00:22,458 --> 00:00:24,510
through their API as well.

10
00:00:25,519 --> 00:00:27,395
And attached, you'll find a link to the API

11
00:00:27,443 --> 00:00:30,056
documentation, which again is unfortunately

12
00:00:30,072 --> 00:00:31,787
just a markdown file on GitHub.

13
00:00:32,895 --> 00:00:34,677
But there you learned that you could also

14
00:00:34,725 --> 00:00:37,407
create a model by sending a POST request to

15
00:00:37,407 --> 00:00:38,515
the right endpoint.

16
00:00:39,141 --> 00:00:41,309
You would have to specify a name for the

17
00:00:41,309 --> 00:00:41,694
model

18
00:00:43,155 --> 00:00:45,708
and then basically specify all the details

19
00:00:45,805 --> 00:00:47,812
you would otherwise put into your model

20
00:00:47,812 --> 00:00:48,149
file,

21
00:00:49,032 --> 00:00:50,300
like the base model,

22
00:00:50,943 --> 00:00:52,243
maybe a template,

23
00:00:52,869 --> 00:00:54,700
parameters or messages,

24
00:00:55,519 --> 00:00:56,787
or a system message.

25
00:00:57,702 --> 00:01:00,716
So you could build a model programmatically.

26
00:01:01,710 --> 00:01:03,986
And of course, for your own use on your

27
00:01:04,034 --> 00:01:06,455
system, you might not wanna do that. Using a

28
00:01:06,455 --> 00:01:09,437
model file and Ollama Create might be more

29
00:01:09,469 --> 00:01:09,870
convenient.

30
00:01:10,768 --> 00:01:12,387
But of course, if you're building some kind

31
00:01:12,387 --> 00:01:14,647
of application which you wanna expose to

32
00:01:14,759 --> 00:01:17,068
other users from all over the world and you

33
00:01:17,100 --> 00:01:19,376
wanna automate the process of building

34
00:01:19,424 --> 00:01:22,070
customized models, then this could be a

35
00:01:22,134 --> 00:01:22,855
useful feature.

36
00:01:23,657 --> 00:01:26,125
And it's not just that. You can really do

37
00:01:26,397 --> 00:01:28,770
everything else as well, including deleting

38
00:01:28,882 --> 00:01:29,972
or pulling models.

39
00:01:30,725 --> 00:01:33,017
You can also generate vector embeddings,

40
00:01:33,049 --> 00:01:34,909
which can be useful if you're building RAG

41
00:01:34,909 --> 00:01:35,422
systems.

42
00:01:36,095 --> 00:01:37,858
But you can, of course, also generate a

43
00:01:37,858 --> 00:01:40,983
completion or a chat completion that takes

44
00:01:40,983 --> 00:01:42,971
